{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43464 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "Alloocimene, (4Z,6Z)- is implicated in the biological activity of HepG2 through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for several enzymes, including Carboxylesterase 2 and RXF 631, which in turn target HepG2. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Alloocimene, (4Z,6Z)- influences HepG2 through the activation of downstream targets. The integration of these relationships underscores a possible role in modulating cellular processes within HepG2 cells, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a network of interactions that may collectively contribute to the observed effects on HepG2, emphasizing the compound's potential as a modulator of hepatic cell function.",
